### Standalone Race on the Main Track

For those interested in experiencing the thrill of racing without purchasing a jump pass, AeroSports Scarborough offers a standalone race option on their main track. This exciting opportunity is priced at nineteen dollars and ninety cents per participant. To ensure safety and an optimal experience for all racers, participants must meet a minimum height requirement of fifty-two inches if they are driving. Each racer can enjoy up to ten laps around the track.

[2] (source: chatbot_quick_replies.md)
### What To Do

**Sample question:** What can I do at AeroSports Scarborough?

**Response:** At AeroSports Scarborough, you'll find a variety of activities to enjoy. The facility features wall-to-wall trampolines, a ninja warrior course, a ninja maze, rock climbing walls, dodgeball, slam basketball, a 360 bicycle ride, giant slides, a jump tower, and go-karting. Note that everything except the go-karting is included in your jump pass.

[3] (source: location_info.md)
## Useful Links

For booking activities or parties, visit the main booking page at https://ecom.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/products/en/home. If you are interested in organizing a birthday party, use this specific link: https://ecom.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/birthdayparties/en/products. To access and complete necessary waivers, go to https://waiver.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/. For directions or to view the location on Google Maps, visit https://g.page/AeroSports-scarborough. Birthday invitations can be created at https://aerosportsinvitation.netlify.app/invitationscarborough.

[4] (source: chatbot_quick_replies.md)
### What Age

**Sample question:** What age can kids come?

**Response:** AeroSports Scarborough welcomes guests of all ages! Children who are able to walk can participate in the activities. Kids under two years old can join for free when accompanied by a paying adult. Additionally, there is a special Toddler Time event on Saturday mornings from nine o'clock until ten o'clock exclusively for children aged five and under, priced at fifteen dollars and ninety cents per child, with one parent allowed to jump for free.

[5] (source: attractions.md)
## Go Karting Thrills

Indoor go-kart racing at AeroSports Scarborough features two tracks: a Main Track designed for taller riders and a Mini Track suitable for younger children. The electric karts allow up to ten laps per race.

- **Age/Height Requirements:** For the Main Track, participants must be at least fifty-two inches tall. For the Mini Track, they must be at least thirty-six inches tall. Closed-toed shoes are required.
- **Included in Jump Pass:** No
- **Pricing Details:** Go-karting requires a separate ticket or can be added as an add-on to your visit. Pricing details can be found on the dedicated Go Karting sheet.


